  }
}



09. scopeQ=/b on CB - the merged Entity is in CP2's scope as well
================================================================
    "id": "urn:V1",


10. Seed urn:V2 on CP1 and on CP2 - the very same single scope /a on both
========================================================================
HTTP/1.1 201 Created
HTTP/1.1 201 Created


11. GET urn:V2 on CB - a union of one Scope renders as a bare String
===================================================================
HTTP/1.1 200 OK
Date: REGEX(.*)
Content-Type: application/json
Link: <https://uri.etsi.org/ngsi-ld/v1/ngsi-ld-core-context-v1.9.jsonld>; rel="http://www.w3.org/ns/json-ld#context"; type="application/ld+json"
Content-Length: REGEX(\d+)

{
  "colour": {
    "type": "Property",
    "value": "blue"
  },
  "id": "urn:V2",
  "scope": "/a",
  "speed": {
    "type": "Property",
    "value": 30
  },
  "type": "Vehicle"
}



12. Re-seed urn:V2 on CP2 WITHOUT any scope
===========================================
HTTP/1.1 204 No Content
Date: REGEX(.*)


HTTP/1.1 201 Created


13. GET urn:V2 on CB - a version without Scopes takes none away: /a
==================================================================
HTTP/1.1 200 OK
Date: REGEX(.*)
Content-Type: application/json
Link: <https://uri.etsi.org/ngsi-ld/v1/ngsi-ld-core-context-v1.9.jsonld>; rel="http://www.w3.org/ns/json-ld#context"; type="application/ld+json"
Content-Length: REGEX(\d+)

{
  "colour": {
    "type": "Property",
    "value": "blue"
  },
  "id": "urn:V2",
  "scope": "/a",
  "speed": {
    "type": "Property",
    "value": 30
  },
  "type": "Vehicle"
}



--TEARDOWN--
swBrokerStop
swBrokerStop -role CP1
swBrokerStop -role CP2
swDbDrop
swDbDrop -role CP1
swDbDrop -role CP2

